The blog uses the same light and dark color palette as the Docs2 theme. CSS custom properties keep each part of the page in step when the theme changes.

## Surfaces

- `--canvas`: the page background.
- `--page`: cards, the header, and dialog panels.
- `--chalk`: inset surfaces, tags, and the footer.

## Text and accent

- `--ink-dark`: headings and prominent labels.
- `--ink-base`: body text.
- `--ink-light`: dates and supporting text.
- `--tab-terracotta`: links, active controls, and focus outlines.
- `--border-strong`: visible dividers and panel borders.

## Using the tokens

Use the custom properties in your CSS so your changes work in both color themes:

```css
.sample-card {
  background: var(--page);
  color: var(--ink-base);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
}

.sample-card a {
  color: var(--tab-terracotta);
}
```
